    "body": "Escalated to effort:high; claim released. No PR opened.\n\nHeld work: branch `issue/1197-workholding-under-fixtures`, commit ab7597f4 (pushed, not merged). Behaviour: the Setups page drops the workholding block and tool list with or without setups; a Setup<n> page gets an \"Open <name> fixtures\" button on its Delete line. Decision note: docs/decisions/1197-workholding-under-fixtures.md.\n\nWhat the quick gate showed:\n- Run 1: the new one-setup test could not click \"Open <name> fixtures\" (below the fold of the default pane), so the Fixtures page never opened.\n- Run 2: a row placed above the button pushed `setup_page_alignment_rows_structure` (\"Pick +X edge\") out of the properties pane, so the button moved onto the Delete line (no new row).\n- Run 3 (head ab7597f4) is green on `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`, and clippy is clean for camcraft-ui. Two failing runs under the worker rule are why this stops rather than opens the PR.\n\nWhy effort:high: the layout limit of the Setup<n> settings page and the click path in the harness need a fresh look (possibly a scrollable settings page or a different place for the pointer), and the pinning test for \"click lands on Fixtures\" is still unproven.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
